A||||4||Gokart||metal under air cleaner.||||4||
Z||000000||Gokart||04-30-2000||05:22 AM||||Has anyone took out their air cleaner lately and looked at the metal support that goes into the tube. Mine was so caked with rust it had little metal left. It took me 3 hours last night with a drill/wire wheel and dremmel/grinding bit to remove it all including the air cleaner housing itself which had plenty on bottom. If it wasn't too late, I would've gone to the hardware store for some muriatic acid. Painted them with Rustoleum primer and will put them back in today. Glad I saw this before the metal totally dissapated! Just tell me this isn't one of those parts GM sells for $20.00 and I wasted all that time!||||reg||4
Z||000001||Standard||05-01-2000||02:36 AM||||Spending 3 hours working on something you love is better than spending $20!  Take pride in your work!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||stsmithgt||05-01-2000||12:01 PM||||I noticed mine was a little rusty this weekend too.  I also noticed the gasket under the air cleaner housing was almost half gone!  Gee wonder where that went?  I'm replacing it with a rubber one instead of using the paper one.  The rubber is tough enough to where it won't get sucked in like the paper did.  I think the paper was holding moisture in there which would do nothing but encourage the rust to thrive.||||reg||9
Z||000003||stsmithgt||05-01-2000||12:04 PM||||I noticed mine was a little rusty this weekend too.  I also noticed the gasket under the air cleaner housing was almost half gone!  Gee wonder where that went?  I'm replacing it with a rubber one instead of using the paper one.  The rubber is tough enough to where it won't get sucked in like the paper did.  I think the paper was holding moisture in there which would do nothing but encourage the rust to thrive.||||reg||9
Z||000004||Gokart||05-01-2000||09:04 PM||||You're so right Standard! I actually enjoyed doing it like any/all time spent with my GT! Replaced that gasket with a "make your own" from a packet containing sheets of cork. Good idea with the rubber! Do they sell it in sheets like the cork?<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||14
